        "name": "control",
        "description": "Control real macOS apps. list returns apps, visible windows and active displays. launch accepts exactly one bundle_id, absolute app_path (.app), or exact app_name; it opens in the background and returns the resolved identity. observe supports mode=ax (Accessibility only, no screenshot or Screen Recording needed), vision (screenshot only), or both (default; AX when available). scope=window (default) requires pid/window_id; scope=app requires pid and composes all its visible windows; scope=screen accepts display_id, defaulting to the main display. Screen scope captures the entire selected display, including other apps. AX elements include their owning pid/window_id; app menu roots carry anchor_window_id instead. Every input requires the latest snapshot_id and consumes it before delivery: observe again before another action. Coordinates are pixels of the returned image, across its full frame; AX-only observations accept elements and explicit screen/normalized coordinates, but no screenshot pixel coordinates. Choose an element or coordinates, never both. press performs AXPress; click/scroll/drag use x/y. Background type/key/keys/paste require a confirmed target element. Background is default for window/app scope; screen input requires delivery=foreground (except AX press). Foreground uses the shared keyboard/mouse. key chords use CMD/CTRL/ALT/SHIFT, e.g. CMD+A or ENTER. dy/dx are signed scroll pixels. sequence executes explicit caller-fixed AX/keyboard steps, while the harness retains task planning and orchestration. hover reveals alternate AX UI or sends a targeted mouse move; moving outside or turn cleanup restores alternate UI. invoke_menu resolves exact path labels afresh after each native expansion, refuses ambiguity/disabled items, and never falls back to pixels. query searches/pages the bounded stored AX tree without renewing input; root_element inspects a subtree and observations optionally include identity-based diffs. set_value writes AXValue; select_text uses an exact unique match with optional prefix/suffix; perform_action invokes a reported AX action. paste supports text/markdown/html, serializes clipboard ownership, and restores it unless another writer changed it. keys sends ordered chords. duration holds input; modifiers and an optional key may be held during click/drag. wait_for requires exact AX expect criteria; wait_for_change combines AX notifications with sampled evidence. Normal wait timeouts return matched/changed=false. after returns fresh evidence; expect on input reports matched/timed_out without replaying it. Input delivery is unverified: observe the result and never blindly retry a write. window manages activate/hide/show by pid+launch_time from list, or raise/minimize/restore/move/resize/close with window_id as well; move uses global screen x/y and resize uses width/height. list include_hidden=true discovers minimized/offscreen windows. isolation conceals an app on an optional virtual display while background input/capture continues; foreground input requires reveal and a fresh observation. status reports OS permissions; permissions requests access for Yakitori Computer.",
        "inputSchema": [
